From: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc64: vdso: map the vvar at the D-cache colour of the kernel data

The L1 D-cache of sun4u CPUs (Spitfire 16K direct mapped, Cheetah and
Jalapeno 64K 4-way) is virtually indexed with 8K pages, so VA bit 13
selects the cache colour. The kernel updates the vDSO time data through
its linear mapping, user space reads it through the [vvar] mapping, whose
address is randomized at page granularity. When the two colours differ,
the write-through stores of the kernel never touch the user's alias lines
and the vDSO keeps reading stale lines until they are displaced.

As seq and cycle_last share one 32-byte line and the clock bases sit in
the next one, the lines go stale independently and the seqcount cannot
detect the mix: on an Ultra 25 (UltraSPARC IIIi, HZ=300) every process
whose vvar has the other colour (about half of them) sees vDSO
CLOCK_MONOTONIC/REALTIME step backwards and forwards by up to 1.6 s,
the user view of seq advances 2-4 times per second instead of 300, and
journald logs "Time jumped backwards, rotating". With user space
displacing the D-cache every round the error shrinks to one tick
(3.3 ms); with a matching colour it is zero.

Map the vvar at the colour of the kernel's mapping of the time page, as
MIPS does for its aliasing caches. sun4v CPUs have no such aliasing.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
---
--- a/arch/sparc/vdso/vma.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/vdso/vma.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <asm/spitfire.h>
 #include <asm/vdso.h>
 #include <asm/page.h>
+#include <asm/shmparam.h>
 
 #include <vdso/datapage.h>
 #include <asm/vdso/vsyscall.h>
@@ -123,6 +124,8 @@ static int map_vdso(const struct vdso_im
 		struct vm_special_mapping *vdso_mapping)
 {
 	const size_t area_size = image->size + VDSO_NR_PAGES * PAGE_SIZE;
+	/* room to move the vvar to the D-cache colour of the kernel data pages */
+	const size_t colour_pad = tlb_type == hypervisor ? 0 : SHMLBA - PAGE_SIZE;
 	struct mm_struct *mm = current->mm;
 	struct vm_area_struct *vma;
 	unsigned long text_start, addr = 0;
@@ -135,19 +138,27 @@ static int map_vdso(const struct vdso_im
 	 * region is free.
 	 */
 	if (current->flags & PF_RANDOMIZE) {
-		addr = get_unmapped_area(NULL, 0, area_size, 0, 0);
+		addr = get_unmapped_area(NULL, 0, area_size + colour_pad, 0, 0);
 		if (IS_ERR_VALUE(addr)) {
 			ret = addr;
 			goto up_fail;
 		}
-		addr = vdso_addr(addr, area_size);
+		addr = vdso_addr(addr, area_size + colour_pad);
 	}
-	addr = get_unmapped_area(NULL, addr, area_size, 0, 0);
+	addr = get_unmapped_area(NULL, addr, area_size + colour_pad, 0, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR_VALUE(addr)) {
 		ret = addr;
 		goto up_fail;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The sun4u L1 D-cache is virtually indexed: a vvar of another colour than
+	 * the kernel's linear mapping keeps stale lines and returns stale time data.
+	 */
+	if (colour_pad)
+		addr += ((unsigned long)vdso_k_time_data -
+			 VDSO_TIME_PAGE_OFFSET * PAGE_SIZE - addr) & (SHMLBA - 1);
+
 	text_start = addr + VDSO_NR_PAGES * PAGE_SIZE;
 	current->mm->context.vdso = (void __user *)text_start;
 
